DESCRIPTION:STATE OF MAINE  APPELLATE DIVISON \nWORKERS’ COMPENSATION BO
 ARD  Case No. App. Div. 26-0007 \n  Decision No. 26-09 \n \nMICHAEL D. KID
 D \n(Appellee) \n \nv. \nAUTOMOBILE CLUB OF SOUTHERN CALIFORNIA \n(Appella
 nt) \n \nand \nCANNON COCHRAN MANAGEMENT SERVS. \n(Insurer) \n \nConferenc
 e held: September 2\, 2026 \nDecided:  September 29\, 2026 \n \nPanel: Adm
 inistrative Law Judges Rooks\, Stovall\, and Hirtle \nBy: Administrative L
 aw Judge Rooks \n \n[¶1]  The Automobile Club of Southern California \, d
 /b/a AAA of Northern \nNew England (“Triple A”)\, appeals from an Admi
 nistrative Law Judge (Sands\, ALJ) \ndecision granting Michael Kidd’s Pe
 tition for Review in part. Triple A contends the \nALJ erred by imputing a
  part-time post-injury earning capacity to Mr. Kidd of \n$450.00 per week 
 . Triple A further a sserts that the medical and labor market \nevidence c
 ompels a finding that Mr. Kidd is able to work full-time with an imputed \
 nearning capacity of $685.60 . We disagree with t hese contentions and aff
 irm the \ndecision.  \nI.  BACKGROUND \n [¶2]  Michael Kidd is a 59-year-
 old resident of the Lewiston-Auburn area. He \nworked for Triple A as a ba
 ttery technician . His job duties involved providing \n2 \n \nroadside ass
 istance to motorists. On February 2\, 2024\, he sustained an injury to his
  \nleft knee while out on a call.  After initial treatment and an MRI that
  show ed an \nabnormality of the medial meniscus\, Mr. Kidd was referred t
 o an orthopedist\, Dr. \nJohn Padavano\, who diagnosed a meniscal tear. Dr
 . Padavano referred Mr. Kidd to \nDr. F. Lincoln Avery for a surgical cons
 ultation. Dr. Avery opined that Mr. Kidd \nmight not have a meniscal tear 
 and recommended conservative treatment.  \n[¶3]  Mr. Kidd was also seen b
 y Dr. Peter Esponette pursuant to 39-A M.R.S. \n§ 207. Dr. Esponnette  re
 commended a further orthopedic consultation to explore \nwhether surgery w
 ould be beneficial  notwithstanding certain preexisting co -\nmorbidities.
  Mr. Kidd went on to see Dr. Stephen Katz\, who diagnosed a probable \nmen
 iscal tea\nhttps://www.maine.gov/wcb/Departments/appellate/2026decisions/2
 6-09%20_Kidd_%20v._%20Automobile_Club_of_S._California_9-29-26.pdf
